ured simultaneously.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bmi-2009-027f1"/></fig><fig id="f2-bmi-2009-027" position="float"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Changes in breath hydrogen after ingestion of distilled water (300 ml, open circle) and hydrogen water (300 ml, 0.4 mM hydrogen, closed circle) in 5 subjects. The difference between the two groups is significant (p &#x0003c; 0.001, two-way analysis of variance).</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bmi-2009-027f2"/></fig><fig id="f3-bmi-2009-027" position="float"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Time course of breath hydrogen by milk (N = 4) and hydrogen water (N = 2 for 0.21, 0.41 and 0.58 mM hydrogen) for 540 min.</p></caption><graphic xlink:href="bmi-2009-027f3"/></fig></floats-group></article>